{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "what": "Data record of the exact Python environment in which the ColPali trial's slice runs and its self-contained CPU reproduction ran. It replaces the installable reproduction/requirements-lock.txt: every pinned line is kept byte-for-byte below, with the original file's sha256 and size, so reproduction/regenerate_lock.py can rebuild an identical lock into a temporary directory, and only when its caller passes --accept-known-advisories.",
  "recorded": "2026-09-26",
  "why_not_a_lockfile": "The environment pins torch 2.8.0 and transformers 4.53.1, which carry the known advisories listed below (1 Critical, 15 High, 4 Medium). colpali-engine 0.3.13, the version vidore-benchmark 5.0.0's colpali-engine extra resolved to, requires torch<2.9.0 and transformers>=4.53.1,<4.58.0 (source-review.json#colpali-engine-deps); every fixed version OSV lists for these advisories is torch 2.9.0 or later or transformers 5.0.0rc3 (a 5.0.0 pre-release) or later, and nine list no fixed version. No patched environment exists inside that range, so the repository keeps what ran as data instead of shipping an installable known-vulnerable environment. No OSV-Scanner ignore was added.",
  "original_lock": {
    "historical_path": "reproduction/requirements-lock.txt",
    "git_revision": "603027b617b4561363a7a79995c9d349de3ea5de",
